From 887e433d8e1582b4f1448045e794f93bcd3f8d29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CanMehEvolve <noreply@example.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Mesg::AddField(const Field&): scan fields directly instead of
 calling GetField

What: loops over the existing fields comparing numbers and returns early on a duplicate, then push_back.
Why it might be faster: avoids the extra call and returned pointer of GetField on a hot path of message construction (about 1.4% at search time).

Provenance: greedy search, seed 3, generation 21, region 226 (Mesg::AddField).
Generated by the model (deepseek-v4.1-flash); not hand-written. Search-time ratio R (candidate/stock, <1 is faster): 0.8770 -> 0.8650 at acceptance (max of two measurements). This is a ranking value, NOT an independent per-patch
confirmation; only the fixed FINAL patch of the run was re-measured independently.
Cumulative patch it was derived from: runs/deepseek/greedy-s3-1072869/patches/gen_21.patch (diff against stock; do not apply together with the others).
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/fit_mesg.cpp | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/fit_mesg.cpp b/src/fit_mesg.cpp
index 6972b9b..73146cc 100644
--- a/src/fit_mesg.cpp
+++ b/src/fit_mesg.cpp
@@ -174,10 +174,15 @@ FIT_BOOL Mesg::HasField(const int fieldNum) const
 
 void Mesg::AddField(const Field& field)
 {
-    Field *existingField = GetField(field.GetNum());
+    const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum = field.GetNum();
 
-    if (existingField == FIT_NULL)
-        fields.push_back(field);
+    for (Field& existing : fields)
+    {
+        if (existing.GetNum() == fieldNum)
+            return;
+    }
+
+    fields.push_back(field);
 }
 
 Field* Mesg::AddField(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
